      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The author describes three observations characterized by the following similar features: 1. Children, between 2 and 9 years, suffering from attacks of sterotyped headaches. 2. EEG with bursts of high- voltage paroxysmal discharges, mainly during hyperventilation. 3. Efficiency of antiepileptic drugs contrary to antimigrainous treatment. These headaches are considered by the author as \"epileptic\", and this diagnosis is discussed."},
